<span class="preheader" style="color: transparent; display: none; height: 0; max-height: 0; max-width: 0; opacity: 0; overflow: hidden; mso-hide: all; visibility: hidden; width: 0;">Compare models with /model, execute with /fleet.</span>

<p class="tmp-mb-3">
  <%= @user_login %>,
</p>

<p class="tmp-mb-3">
  You now have access to GitHub <%= Copilot::Policies::Cli.display_name %> through your organization
  <%= link_to @organization_login, user_url(@organization_login) %>.
</p>

<p class="tmp-mb-3">
  <strong>Get started: <%= link_to "https://gh.io/copilot-cli-quickstart", "https://gh.io/copilot-cli-quickstart" %></strong>
</p>

<p class="tmp-mb-3">
  <%= link_to "Watch our quickstart video ›", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=nSLmfGC7DkI" %>
</p>

<p class="tmp-mb-3">
  Then try it on a real issue by using Shift+Tab to enter plan mode.
  From there you can:
</p>

<ul>
  <li>Use /model to compare approaches across models</li>
  <li>Run /fleet to execute across multiple models in parallel</li>
  <li>Open the work in your /IDE and ship a pull request</li>
</ul>

<p class="tmp-mb-3">
  <strong>All inside your existing repositories, issues, and pull request workflows.</strong> Use /changelog to stay on top of what's new in <%= Copilot::Policies::Cli.display_name %>.
</p>

<p class="tmp-mb-3">
  <%= link_to "Learn more in Docs ›", "https://docs.github.com/en/copilot/how-tos/copilot-cli/cli-best-practices" %>
</p>

<p class="tmp-mb-3">
  For more information on setting up and using GitHub Copilot, visit the
  <%= link_to "feedback forum", Copilot::COPILOT_FEEDBACK_FORUM %> or
  <%= link_to "read the documentation", Copilot::COPILOT_DOCUMENTATION %>.
</p>

<% content_for :footer_text do %>
  <p>
    You are receiving this because you are the owner of the <%= link_to @user_login, user_url(@user_login) %> account.
  </p>
